   "text": "Free Decay of a Linearly Damped Oscillator: A Benchmark Note"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i1",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46162,
    "y": 0.22284,
    "w": 0.07677,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "C. Bench"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i2",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44393,
    "y": 0.25372,
    "w": 0.11215,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "October 2026"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i3",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46419,
    "y": 0.3066,
    "w": 0.07163,
    "h": 0.01258
   },
   "text": "Abstract"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i4",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.17398,
    "y": 0.3305,
    "w": 0.65205,
    "h": 0.04277
   },
   "text": "A unit-mass, unit-stiffness oscillator with viscous damping coefficient 0.5 is released from rest conditions in the bench fixture. We record the decay envelope and the zero crossings of the displacement x with velocity y."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i5",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.39965,
    "w": 0.27068,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "1 Equations of motion"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i6",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.43391,
    "w": 0.36445,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "With the state vector (x, y) the dynamics read"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i7",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.47586,
    "y": 0.46485,
    "w": 0.39473,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { x } = y ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i8",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44047,
    "y": 0.4958,
    "w": 0.43012,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { y } = - x - 0 . 5 \\, y ."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i9",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.53572,
    "w": 0.24916,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "2 Release conditions"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i10",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.56998,
    "w": 0.74119,
    "h": 0.04799
   },
   "text": "The arm is clamped at a displacement of one and a half units and released from rest: the initial state is x(0) = 1.5 and y(0) = 0. The motion is underdamped, so the amplitude envelope decays geometrically while the sign of x alternates each half period."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i11",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.64412,
    "w": 0.19344,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "3 Stability note"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i12",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.67838,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "Both eigenvalues have negative real part, so every trajectory converges to the origin regardless of the release displacement."
  }
 ]
}